## {{PROJECT_NAME}} Go server

Module: `{{MODULE_PATH}}`. The starter uses Go's standard HTTP library and has no
external service dependencies. The `go.mod` directive records the Go toolchain
used to initialize it. If the module begins with `example.com/`, it is a local
placeholder; set your real repository module path and update imports before
publishing or sharing it as a module.

Run locally:

```bash
go run ./cmd/api
curl http://localhost:8080/health
```

`HTTP_ADDR` defaults to `:8080`; set it to use another address. `GET /health`
returns `200` with `{"status":"ok"}` and checks process liveness only.
The server has HTTP timeouts and handles interrupt/SIGTERM for graceful shutdown.

The layout and all future feature rules are in [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md). Start a
feature by requesting `add-go-feature <feature description>`, or simply describe
the feature while working in this project. Implement business operations through
domain, use case, adapter, and composition layers. The empty domain, usecase,
and repository directories are reserved for actual business behavior.

Validate changes:

```bash
go build ./...
go test ./...
go vet ./...
```

The architecture is informed by
[geusan/go-clean-arch-chat-server](https://github.com/geusan/go-clean-arch-chat-server),
with framework-specific types kept outside business code.
